{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Elohim remembered Noah, etc.</b> The reason He did not limit Himself to mentioning Noah alone and added to say <b>and et every living creature</b> — perhaps it comes to inform us even regarding the living creatures and beasts that were with Him alone, it would have sufficed for Him to remember; and the meaning of the matter is in the manner of 'not only this but also that.'" "<b>Further,</b> it intends along this line: <b>And Elohim remembered Noah</b> — He also took account of all the burden and weight that was upon him from the beasts and living creatures, etc., that were with him in the ark, and had compassion upon him. In this too He included an allusion to the trouble that befell Noah (Tanchuma) from a lion that bit him, endangering him in the ark on account of the abundance of added worry, etc. And likewise the withholding of remedy for his ailment. Thus you would say that the essence of the remembrance is for Noah." "<b>And Elohim caused a wind to pass, etc.</b> The intention is to inform us that HaShem commanded the waters to surge, just as He commanded them during the six days of Creation (Genesis 1:20): ״יִשְׁרְצוּ הַמַּיִם״ — so too He commanded them here to act with might. And therefore you will find that after all existence had been blotted out, the verse says <b>and the waters prevailed</b>, etc., and that is with no need, for even the unformed bodies of the created beings had already been blotted out. The reason is that the waters were engaged in the command that HaShem had decreed upon them, and they have no mandate to seek interpretations to hold back their surging after all existence had been blotted out, until HaShem remembered Noah and then commanded the waters to be calmed from their surging. And that is what the verse says: <b>and Elohim caused a wind to pass</b> — a spirit of kindness and compassion, and the forces of the waters were sweetened. And this is what Onkelos translated ״וַיָּשֹׁכּוּ הַמָּיִם״ — ״וְנָחוּ מַיָּא״ — that they surged no more."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:10.869554474Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}